{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310603,"nonce":"T+vwNNta96n/FvtlgnEP854crek=","title":"CONVENTION + FIX (2026-09-05): an erased type parameter `T` carries RAW bits (like erased formals); `Null\u003cT\u003e` from a `get()` is a BOX. ...","message":"**Landed:** commits 72b574b4 (devirt env) af61b4fb (map slot adapters) edd52081 (KeyValueIterator protocol) a7c1041c (erased Null\u003cT\u003e boundaries) 721e10d0 (typer IMap identity); battery 439/439 vs conf_d9c, GAINED Issue3635 / LOST Issue12700 both bistable on one binary (12700: 2/5 PASS).\n\n**The case:** upstream `MapKeyValueIterator.next` is `{value: @:nullSafety(Off) (map.get(key) : V), key: key}`.\n`get` returns a `Null\u003cV\u003e` box (the extern-map adapter probes `exists` and boxes, D10 shape);\nthe CHECK-TYPE `(e : V)` is `TypedExpressionKind::Cast{Checked}` → `casts.rs` had no\n`(Optional, TypeParameter)` arm ⇒ box passed through ⇒ the consumer, typed `Int`, read the\npointer. `casts.rs` now routes `(Dynamic|Optional) → TypeParameter` through\n`haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr` (box → payload, else the address); `literals.rs` does the same for\nan erased field fed a box. Interface receivers now substitute their type args\n(`compute_type_substitution` got an `Interface` arm + interfaces record `set_class_type_params`),\nso `map.get(k)` types as `Null\u003cV'\u003e`, not `NoChange(Null\u003cV_imap\u003e)`.\n\n**Gaps (recorded, not fixed):**\n1. FIXED 2026-09-05: the wrap site hands the value's static type to `wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr_for`; `get` adapters are minted per value kind (`__int/__bool/__float`, raw pointer for refs, int box only when erased). Was: the map `get` adapter boxes the raw u64 as an INT box for ANY V (`haxe_box_int_ptr`); a typed\n   caller with V=String/Float/Bool gets the wrong box. The erased consumer is fine (payload = raw bits).\n2. `haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr` decides \"is a box\" by reading the first word of any 8-aligned heap\n   pointer and comparing with TYPE_INT(3)/TYPE_BOOL(2). A HaxeString's first word is its data\n   pointer (safe); an anon object's is its shape id (small — collision possible).\n\n**Tools:** `RAYZOR_IFACE_DIAG=1` (`[fatptr]`, `[resolved-call]`), `RAYZOR_SYM_DEBUG=1`\n(`[sym] import-placeholder / pre-register iface / lower iface / type-path / member-synth` + candidate list),\n`RAYZOR_FORIN_DEBUG=1` (`[for-in] ty kind protocol`). See [[bugs-imap-never-loads-generic-subtype-import]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_erased_null_t_box_at_type_param_boundary` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}